* Raspberry Pi Pico (RP2040): I2C bus with an LM75 and an LCD 16x2 I2C (PCF8574)
* Run from this folder:  ngspice pico_i2c_test.cir
* Firmware: ../firmware/pico/pico_i2c.bin (make -C ../firmware/pico)
* The I2C frames are electrical: GP4 = SDA, GP5 = SCL (open drain, 100 kHz),
* 4.7 kohm pull-ups to 3.3 V; the slaves pull SDA low for ACK and data.

* Models generated for this firmware:
*   python3 ../tools/make_pico_lib.py --relative --fw ../firmware/pico/pico_i2c.bin \
*       --name i2c --so ../build/mcu_cosim.so -o pico_i2c.lib
*   python3 ../tools/make_i2c_lib.py --relative --lm75 0x48 --lcd 0x27 --log \
*       --so ../build/mcu_cosim.so -o i2c_slaves.lib
.include pico_i2c.lib
.include i2c_slaves.lib

*     GP0 GP1 GP2 GP3 GP4 GP5 GP6 GP7 GP8 GP9 GP10 GP11 GP12 GP13 GP14 GP15 GP16
XP    tx  rx  n2  n3  sda scl n6  n7  n8  n9  n10  n11  n12  n13  n14  n15  n16
*     GP17 GP18 GP19 GP20 GP21 GP22 GP26 GP27 GP28 VBUS VSYS V3V3_EN V3V3 ADC_VREF RUN
+     n17  n18  n19  n20  n21  n22  n26  n27  n28  vbus vsys en      v33  vref     run  PICO_I2C

*      GND VCC SDA SCL
XI2C   0   v33 sda scl I2C_SLAVES

* Pull-ups of the bus, and the capacitance of the wires (about 50 pF)
Rsda sda v33 4.7k
Rscl scl v33 4.7k
Csda sda 0 50p
Cscl scl 0 50p
* UART: receiver load on TX, RX idle high
Rtx tx 0 100k
Rrx rx v33 10k

.control
tran 0.5u 30m
plot v(scl) v(sda)+4 xlimit 0 1m
.endc
.end
